  ==================================================== -->
  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <div class="c">
      <span class="eyebrow">Common Questions</span>
      <h2 class="h2" id="faq-h2">Apparel Manufacturer Bangladesh — Questions Buyers Ask About SDF Clothing</h2>
      <div style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-q">What is the minimum order quantity for apparel production?</div>
          <div class="faq-a"><strong>300 pieces per style</strong> — across OEM, private label, CMT, and ODM production. Size distribution within the 300 pieces is flexible. If you are ordering multiple styles on the same purchase order, each style has its own 300-piece minimum. We accept first-time brand orders at 300 pieces per style — no trial order surcharges, no higher MOQ for new clients.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-q">How does SDF Clothing compare to other apparel manufacturers in Bangladesh?</div>
          <div class="faq-a">Three differences most clients mention: first, <strong>300 pieces MOQ</strong> — most Bangladesh apparel factories start at 500–1,000 pieces. Second, <strong>full-chain GOTS certification</strong> — most factories use organic cotton but cannot provide GOTS chain-of-custody for your organic labelling claim. Third, <strong>EU EPR 2026 / DPP readiness</strong> — we generate Digital Product Passport data files as standard. Most Bangladesh factories are not yet doing this. Beyond those, direct factory access — no agents — means pricing transparency that buying house models cannot match.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-q">What is the typical lead time from order to shipment?</div>
          <div class="faq-a">Proto sample: <strong>14 days</strong> from confirmed brief, shipped DHL Express. Pre-production sample: 10 days after proto approval. Bulk production: <strong>30–45 days</strong> from PP sample sign-off. Total first-order time from brief to FOB Chittagong: approximately 55–65 days. Repeat orders run faster as fabric and PP samples are already approved. Ocean freight to EU ports (Genova, Hamburg, Rotterdam): 22–28 days additional transit.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-q">Do EU fashion brands pay import duty on apparel from SDF Clothing?</div>
          <div class="faq-a"><strong>No.</strong> Bangladesh holds EU GSP EBA (Everything But Arms) status — 0% import duty on most apparel categories (HS chapters 61 and 62) into all 27 EU member states. Standard EU MFN duty is 12% of CIF value — on a €100,000 order, that is €12,000 saved. We prepare the EUR.1 Movement Certificate for every EU shipment. Your Italian, German, French, Dutch, or Swedish customs agent receives a complete document pack. <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-italy">Read our Italy page</a> or <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-germany">Germany page</a> for country-specific customs detail.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-q">Can I visit the SDF Clothing factory in Bangladesh?</div>
          <div class="faq-a">Yes. Factory visits are welcome for verified business partners — we encourage them. Third-party social and environmental audits at our facility are also supported: SGS, Bureau Veritas, and Intertek all conduct audits here. If your retail buyer has a specific audit format requirement, we work with you to schedule it. We have nothing to hide — factory transparency is a basic expectation, not a favour.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-q">Does SDF Clothing work with startup fashion brands or only established labels?</div>
          <div class="faq-a">Both. The 300-piece MOQ specifically exists to make factory-direct apparel manufacturing accessible to brands that are not yet ordering at scale. A founder placing their debut collection at 300 pieces per style gets the same factory, same certifications, same quality control process, and same compliance documentation as a brand ordering 50,000 pieces. The price per piece differs with volume — the production standard does not.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-q">What apparel categories does SDF Clothing specialise in?</div>
          <div class="faq-a">We produce across all major apparel categories: knitwear and jersey (t-shirts, sweaters, polo shirts, jersey dresses), woven shirts and blouses, dresses, trousers, outerwear and jackets, activewear, loungewear, sleepwear, and children's apparel. Knitwear is Bangladesh's highest-volume export category and a particular strength — organic cotton knitwear for EU brands is a core production line. All categories available from 300 pieces with GOTS, OEKO-TEX, or GRS certification as required.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

